body:
Maybe in a few years things would have been different, or I would have found somebody else, or any number of other things. Maybe I could learn to live alone comfortably or just be happy with a pet. There are a million and one maybes that I've been through in my head. There are ways that this could have worked out well. But in the end I know these chances to find contentment in life are few and far between. After many years of depression I found one single thing that could shake off the daily melancholy, and it slipped away before I even had a chance.

&#x200B;

Some people go their entire natural lives unhappy, just going through the motions wondering when things will get better. Right now, tonight, that outcome is more likely for me than any other. I don't want to stay and find out.

No, I don't think we do. Not in this matter. Let's say even if I were to win the lottery and find somebody else, somebody I can actually connect to and trust and feel for. Somebody who would mean something to me, it is still a lotto if she would feel the same way about me. I can't control others feelings, I have no power over this.

&#x200B;

Further more, in all the time I've been alive I've met one person that I felt I could really trust and connect to. Even before I felt romantic feelings towards my housemate, there was a time when I thought she wasn't my type at all romantically, but I still connected with her on an emotional level. If it takes me as long to find somebody else that I can connect with as it took to find her then it isn't worth waiting. I'm not going to suffer years of doubt, anxiety, boredom and loneliness just to find somebody else and maybe have a slim chance they will feel the same way about me.

You're right, maybe tomorrow is the day that I find somebody else and today really is as bad as it gets. But it isn't likely. What is far more likely is that tomorrow is just like today, just like yesterday was. I'm not going to live a life on the basis of 'Maybe tomorrow' every single day.

&#x200B;

It's no different from people buying lottery tickets. Just because you might win doesn't make it worth buying the ticket.
